            {
              "id": "GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Next.js HTTP request deserialization can lead to DoS when using insecure React Server Components"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability affects certain React Server Components packages for versions 19.0.x, 19.1.x, and 19.2.x and frameworks that use the affected packages, including Next.js 13.x, 14.x, 15.x, and 16.x using the App Router. The issue is tracked upstream as [CVE-2026-23864](https://github.com/facebook/react/security/advisories/GHSA-83fc-fqcc-2hmg).\n\nA specially crafted HTTP request can be sent to any App Router Server Function endpoint that, when deserialized, may trigger excessive CPU usage, out-of-memory exceptions, or server crashes. This can result in denial of service in unpatched environments."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: next\nFixed Version: 15.0.8, 15.1.12, 15.2.9, 15.3.9, 15.4.11, 15.5.10, 15.6.0-canary.61, 16.0.11, 16.1.5\nLink: [GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf)\nA vulnerability affects certain React Server Components packages for versions 19.0.x, 19.1.x, and 19.2.x and frameworks that use the affected packages, including Next.js 13.x, 14.x, 15.x, and 16.x using the App Router. The issue is tracked upstream as [CVE-2026-23864](https://github.com/facebook/react/security/advisories/GHSA-83fc-fqcc-2hmg).\n\nA specially crafted HTTP request can be sent to any App Router Server Function endpoint that, when deserialized, may trigger excessive CPU usage, out-of-memory exceptions, or server crashes. This can result in denial of service in unpatched environments.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|next|15.0.8, 15.1.12, 15.2.9, 15.3.9, 15.4.11, 15.5.10, 15.6.0-canary.61, 16.0.11, 16.1.5|[GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf)|\n\nA vulnerability affects certain React Server Components packages for versions 19.0.x, 19.1.x, and 19.2.x and frameworks that use the affected packages, including Next.js 13.x, 14.x, 15.x, and 16.x using the App Router. The issue is tracked upstream as [CVE-2026-23864](https://github.com/facebook/react/security/advisories/GHSA-83fc-fqcc-2hmg).\n\nA specially crafted HTTP request can be sent to any App Router Server Function endpoint that, when deserialized, may trigger excessive CPU usage, out-of-memory exceptions, or server crashes. This can result in denial of service in unpatched environments."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Next Vulnerable to Denial of Service with Server Components"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability affects certain React packages for versions 19.0.0, 19.0.1, 19.1.0, 19.1.1, 19.1.2, 19.2.0, and 19.2.1 and frameworks that use the affected packages, including Next.js 15.x and 16.x using the App Router. The issue is tracked upstream as [CVE-2025-55184](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-55184).\n\nA malicious HTTP request can be crafted and sent to any App Router endpoint that, when deserialized, can cause the server process to hang and consume CPU. This can result in denial of service in unpatched environments."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: next\nFixed Version: 14.2.34, 15.0.6, 15.1.10, 15.2.7, 15.3.7, 15.4.9, 15.5.8, 15.6.0-canary.59, 16.0.9, 16.1.0-canary.17\nLink: [GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c)\nA vulnerability affects certain React packages for versions 19.0.0, 19.0.1, 19.1.0, 19.1.1, 19.1.2, 19.2.0, and 19.2.1 and frameworks that use the affected packages, including Next.js 15.x and 16.x using the App Router. The issue is tracked upstream as [CVE-2025-55184](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-55184).\n\nA malicious HTTP request can be crafted and sent to any App Router endpoint that, when deserialized, can cause the server process to hang and consume CPU. This can result in denial of service in unpatched environments.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|next|14.2.34, 15.0.6, 15.1.10, 15.2.7, 15.3.7, 15.4.9, 15.5.8, 15.6.0-canary.59, 16.0.9, 16.1.0-canary.17|[GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-mwv6-3258-q52c)|\n\nA vulnerability affects certain React packages for versions 19.0.0, 19.0.1, 19.1.0, 19.1.1, 19.1.2, 19.2.0, and 19.2.1 and frameworks that use the affected packages, including Next.js 15.x and 16.x using the App Router. The issue is tracked upstream as [CVE-2025-55184](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-55184).\n\nA malicious HTTP request can be crafted and sent to any App Router endpoint that, when deserialized, can cause the server process to hang and consume CPU. This can result in denial of service in unpatched environments."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-57822",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Next.js Improper Middleware Redirect Handling Leads to SSRF"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Next.js is a React framework for building full-stack web applications. Prior to versions 14.2.32 and 15.4.7, when next() was used without explicitly passing the request object, it could lead to SSRF in self-hosted applications that incorrectly forwarded user-supplied headers. This vulnerability has been fixed in Next.js versions 14.2.32 and 15.4.7. All users implementing custom middleware logic in self-hosted environments are strongly encouraged to upgrade and verify correct usage of the next() function."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-57822",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-57822\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: next\nFixed Version: 14.2.32, 15.4.7\nLink: [CVE-2025-57822](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-57822)\nNext.js is a React framework for building full-stack web applications. Prior to versions 14.2.32 and 15.4.7, when next() was used without explicitly passing the request object, it could lead to SSRF in self-hosted applications that incorrectly forwarded user-supplied headers. This vulnerability has been fixed in Next.js versions 14.2.32 and 15.4.7. All users implementing custom middleware logic in self-hosted environments are strongly encouraged to upgrade and verify correct usage of the next() function.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-57822**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|next|14.2.32, 15.4.7|[CVE-2025-57822](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-57822)|\n\nNext.js is a React framework for building full-stack web applications. Prior to versions 14.2.32 and 15.4.7, when next() was used without explicitly passing the request object, it could lead to SSRF in self-hosted applications that incorrectly forwarded user-supplied headers. This vulnerability has been fixed in Next.js versions 14.2.32 and 15.4.7. All users implementing custom middleware logic in self-hosted environments are strongly encouraged to upgrade and verify correct usage of the next() function."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
